{
	"name": "Banner of the Last Stand",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/sundries/flags/banner-standard-moon.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>The Banner of the Last Stand is a powerful magical relic made from the banner of a long-dead hero of a bygone age. Blessed by priests, it is said to carry some small fragment of their spirit, of who they were, in life. When you find this banner roll [[/r 1d10]] to determine how many charges it has. On a 10, reroll and take the new result. It has the following benefits which do not require activation, only that you hold it in your hand:</p><ul><li>Prestige Rating increased by 2</li><li>Provides a +5 bonus to AC instead of the typical +3 of a very rare banner.</li><li>When held aloft during a forced march, creatures within 120ft do not need to make Constitution saves for up to 24 hours of continuous forced march, but gain 1 fatigue for every 12 hours of forced march they perform.</li></ul><p>In addition, if you are a @UUID[Compendium.a5e-martial-artistry.classes.Item.QNkTfOZJVncpKef2]{Champion} engaging in a quest, you may gain the benefits of a long rest after completing a short rest, once. This does not end your quest.</p><p>Finally, this banner can inspire a last stand. By expending 10 charges while bloodied, you initiate a last stand. When you do so, you become doomed and will perish at the end of the encounter. While the last stand persists you gain advantage on attack rolls and saving throws, and you ignore the incapacitated condition. The last stand ends after 1 minute or when combat does, whichever happens first.</p>",
